# Example 24: Spatial dFBA - substrate-gradient colony growth (S6)
# A one-dimensional strip of well-mixed dynamic-FBA batches is coupled
# by glucose diffusion, with a glucose reservoir held at the inlet site
# (site 0).  Growth at each site consumes local glucose via a
# Michaelis-Menten uptake bound and an instantaneous FBA LP, the static
# optimization approach of Mahadevan et al. 2002 (Biophys J 83:1905).
# The diffusion coefficient is the biofilm-effective value (Rittmann &
# McCarty, Environmental Biotechnology, 2020): glucose in free solution
# diffuses ~600 um^2/s, but biofilms reduce it by orders of magnitude.
#
# The result is a plug-flow-reactor pattern: a substrate-depletion
# boundary layer at the inlet (continuous resupply), a graded decline
# of biomass with distance, and a large CO2 overflow (the reduced core
# model has no glyoxylate shunt, so no acetate / second growth phase).
#
#gene name=glucose_uptake
ATG GCT GGT GTA TAA
#end
#
#config length=32 inlet=5.0 diffusion_um2_s=2.0 output=stdout
#
